NNAAMMEE
     ttttyyffllaaggss — set device-specific flags for terminals

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ttttyyffllaaggss [--ppvv] [--aa | _t_t_y _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ttttyyffllaaggss sets the device-specific flags for terminals, based on the flags
     found on the terminal's line in _/_e_t_c_/_t_t_y_s.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa      Set the flags for all terminals in _/_e_t_c_/_t_t_y_s.

     --pp      Print out flag information about each terminal, instead of set‐
             ting anything.

     --vv      Be verbose about what the terminal's flags will be set to.

     The _t_t_y arguments are optional, but must not be specified if the --aa flag
     is used.  If specified, the _t_t_y arguments should be the base names of the
     ttys, as found in _/_e_t_c_/_t_t_y_s.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/ttys

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     getttyent(3), ttys(5)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ttttyyffllaaggss utility appeared in NetBSD 0.9A.

BBUUGGSS
     The conditions on which to report an error are ill-defined.  ttttyyffllaaggss
     tries to report all significant errors, perhaps going over-board at
     times.

